ackle in  rise of iron archons forge will feature  rounds that are shorter than prison of  elders but more robust than Court of  Oryx the arena will unlock at the  completion of the campaign missions and  is triggered by using siva offerings  much like the runes required for court  of Oryx rounds in archons forge end with  a boss that drops exclusive gear Bungie  have emphasized the collaborative nature  of this mode as it allows your fire team  to work together with other random  players speaking of gear buns your  overhauling the way artifacts work rise  of iron will introduce eight new  artifacts that can be equipped by any  class each artifact is tied to one of  the iron Lords and will carry unique  abilities for example one particular  artifact will allow you to briefly gain  an enemy's allegiance by punching them  in the face while another will add the  ability to deflect energy-based  projectiles with swords you may remember  a guardian wielding a flaming acts in  the rise of iron announcement trailer  this weapon is actually a relic you come  across during your time in the new  expansion the flaming axe reach I  mo when doing light attacks and expense  mo faster when doing heavy attacks if  you can keep the ammo above a certain  level however the relic will deal double  damage as with all destiny expansions  the light level cap will be increased  this time to 385 with all gear from the  taken King onwards being scaled to match  the cap will be raised to 400 a few  weeks after launch to coincide with the  release of the hard mode rise of iron  raid there are also new cosmetic items  which are basically skins you can apply  to weapons and armor Bungie have also  confirmed that the Halloween celebration  festival of the Lost and sparrow racing  league timed events will be coming back  to destiny after rise of iron launches  rise of iron is the fourth expansion to  hit destiny since its launch in 2014 it  will be the first expansion to release  for current-gen consoles only and will  be available on sep tember 20th for all  the info on rise of iron and everything  swords and magic in space keep your  sights on gamespot
 

